.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt NQSELFTEST 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqselftest
.Nd known answers for every algorithm family
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqselftest void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqselftest
runs fixed inputs through the public functions of every algorithm
family and compares what they produce with answers built into the
library, the kind of self-test a cryptographic module runs before it is
used (FIPS 140-3, section 7.10):
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
SHA-224 to SHA-512/256, SHA3-224 to SHA3-512, SHAKE128 and SHAKE256 of
.Dq abc ;
.It
HMAC-SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA-512 (RFC 4231, test case 2);
.It
ML-KEM-512, -768 and -1024: a key pair and an encapsulation from fixed
seeds, and the decapsulation;
.It
ML-DSA-44, -65 and -87: a key pair from a fixed seed, the deterministic
signature of a fixed message and its verification;
.It
SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f and SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128f: a key pair from a fixed seed;
.It
HQC-128: a key pair, an encapsulation and the decapsulation;
.It
Ed25519 and ML-DSA-44+Ed25519: a key pair, a deterministic signature and
its verification.
.El
.Pp
Each family's keys, ciphertexts, signatures, secrets and return codes
are hashed with SHA-256; a decapsulation or verification that disagrees
changes the hash.
The masked decapsulations and signers run as in normal use.
It takes about a tenth of a second and allocates nothing.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
when every answer matches;
.Dv NQEKAT
when one does not.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-selftest 1 ,
.Xr nqerr 3
